<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21183] fid2path on a server node without a client mount</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21183</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Tools that run on a server, such as &lt;tt&gt;lfs find --device --fid2path&lt;/tt&gt; (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20637" title="LFU: Output Format module to generate pathnames from FIDs" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20637"&gt;LU-20637&lt;/a&gt;), need a client mount on that node to turn a FID into a pathname. A client mount on a server node causes problems with HA failover and with module removal.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Add a device-level administrative interface on the target itself, so that basic operations such as &lt;tt&gt;OBD_IOC_FID2PATH&lt;/tt&gt; can be called without a client mount. Possible forms (from review of &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/68288):" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/68288):&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;/mnt/testfs-MDT0000/.lustre/fid/&lt;/tt&gt; on the target mount&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;an ioctl on the target mount point &lt;tt&gt;/mnt/testfs-MDT0000&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;an ioctl on &lt;tt&gt;/dev/obd&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;lfs find --fid2path&lt;/tt&gt; and llapi_scan_rec_path() would then use it when no client mount is given.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
